<header><p class="st-kicker">other · Germany and Central Europe</p><h1 class="st-title">Lusatian League</h1><p class="st-meta">1346 CE – 1815 CE</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">An alliance of six Upper Lusatian towns, formed in 1346, that dominated the politics and trade of their province for centuries.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>In 1346 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bautzen">Bautzen</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gorlitz">Görlitz</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zittau">Zittau</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kamenz">Kamenz</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lobau">Löbau</a> and Lauban, towns of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/margraviate-of-upper-lusatia">Margraviate of Upper Lusatia</a>, then a land of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-bohemia">Kingdom of Bohemia</a>, formed a league to suppress robber knights and protect their trade. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-iv-duke-of-anjou">Charles IV</a>, as king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bohemia">Bohemia</a>, approved the alliance, which became a permanent political force.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The six towns met in regular diets, kept a common treasury and troops, and formed a separate estate in the Upper Lusatian diet alongside the nobility. Their wealth came from cloth and linen weaving and from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/via-regia">Via Regia</a> trade road through <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gorlitz">Görlitz</a>. They fought the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hussites">Hussites</a> in the 15th century and mostly turned Lutheran in the 16th.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 1547 Ferdinand I punished the towns for refusing aid in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/schmalkaldic-war">Schmalkaldic War</a>, confiscating lands and privileges. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/upper-lusatia">Upper Lusatia</a> passed to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/electorate-of-saxony">Electorate of Saxony</a> in 1635, and the league lingered until 1815, when <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gorlitz">Görlitz</a> and Lauban went to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-prussia">Prussia</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="other, 1346 CE – 1815 CE"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M24 82 V42 H32 V34 H40 V42 H46 V34 H54 V42 H60 V34 H68 V42 H76 V82 Z"/><path d="M44 82 V66 Q50 58 56 66 V82"/><path d="M34 54 H40 M60 54 H66"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">other</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Germany and Central Europe</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:86.49%;width:9.33%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1346 CE – 1815 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>other</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>mercantile</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Lutheranism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>German, Sorbian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/germany">Germany</a>, <a href="/countries/poland">Poland</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Six Towns League, Oberlausitzer Sechsstädtebund</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1580&amp;focus=lusatian-league" aria-label="Lusatian League on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4884 401 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Lusatian League lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5325 660h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5204 657h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M5204 657h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day Germany. <a href="/atlas?year=1580&amp;focus=lusatian-league">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

